menuconfig MANAGER_OXM
    bool "OVSDB Translator (OXM)"
    depends on OS_TR181_LIB && !OS_TR181_LIB_NULL
    default y
    help
        This option enables the OVSDB Translator (OXM) manager which projects
        OVSDB into TR-181 data model and back.

        This allows integrating legacy Opensync systems that were exclusively
        designed to operate over OVSDB, with the new TR-181 based data model.

        By enabling this manager, you can ensure that your existing OVSDB-based
        configurations and operations continue to function seamlessly while
        transitioning to the TR-181 data model.

        If unsure, select 'y'.

    config MANAGER_OXM_CFG
        depends on MANAGER_OXM
        string "Startup configuration"
        default "oxm;true;needs_plan_b=false;max_memory=100000"
        help
            This option allows you to specify the startup configuration for the
            OVSDB Translator (OXM) manager.
            Optional crash backoff keys (;-separated key=value):
            crash_count_max, crash_count_period, crash_recovery.
            crash_count_max=0 disables. Ignored when needs_plan_b=true.
